---
import DocsPage from "../../../components/DocsPage.astro";

const description = "Upgrading from @derpdaderp/chartkit and the prop-based dashboard components to the v1 JSON spec.";
const shell = `npm uninstall @derpdaderp/chartkit
npm install @chartkitdev/react @chartkitdev/core`;
---

<DocsPage title="Upgrading from v0" description={description} href="/docs/migrate">
  <p>
    v0 was the React component library <code>@derpdaderp/chartkit</code>. v1 is a JSON spec. React, Vue, Svelte, vanilla DOM, and Node render that same object.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="opt-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Before</th>
          <th>After</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@derpdaderp/chartkit</code></td>
          <td><code>@chartkitdev/react</code> for components, <code>@chartkitdev/core</code> for the spec</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Component props such as dataKey and leftAxis</td>
          <td>A spec: version, type, data, encoding, a11y.alt</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>React only</td>
          <td>React, Vue, Svelte, vanilla, and renderToString</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <figure class="code"><figcaption>shell</figcaption><pre><code>{shell}</code></pre></figure>
  <p>
    <code>@chartkitdev/react</code> still exports <code>LineChart</code>, <code>KpiCard</code>, and the other dashboard components. Their props are not spec keys. New charts pass <code>spec</code> to <code>Chart</code>. <code>@derpdaderp/chartkit</code> remains a compatibility shim for existing imports.
  </p>
  <p>
    From another library: <a href="/docs/migrate/chartjs">Chart.js</a>, <a href="/docs/migrate/recharts">Recharts</a>, <a href="/docs/migrate/echarts">ECharts</a>.
  </p>
</DocsPage>
